<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA3-QA1-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA3-QA1-004" ;
  triage:title "Task 4's documented no-delivery-channel Hold behavior is not implemented anywhere; its only test is one of the hollow BA3-QA1-002 aliases" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (req-qa), PR #1402 @ c13f9bddf, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643113496. Task 4's documented behavior (Hold(\"no delivery channel\"), one warn per tick) is not implemented anywhere: build_task_reminder_dispatch's Ok(None) case is a bare return with no disposition or log line, and no \"no delivery channel\" string exists in the crate. Its supposed test, member_without_dispatchable_backend_holds_and_logs_once, is one of the hollow aliases from BA3-QA1-002, so this gap shipped undetected. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1402#issuecomment-5643134050): STANDS; folded into BA3-FIX-R3-1789183410 with its test." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake_reminders.rs (build_task_reminder_dispatch)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T03:23:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:relatedFinding "BA3-QA1-002" ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix's cleanup ruling (ATM 2026-09-12T04:44:29Z) adds worktree layer 5, fix/phase-ba-cleanup (new gh-stack layer above docs/ba6, cipher single writer, pushed at BA.6's then-current head a49b922aa; now dfd47edca). No longer folded into BA3-FIX-R3 on feature/ba3-nudge-invariant -- fixed once on fix/phase-ba-cleanup per the O(n^2) fix-multiplication avoidance rule; the ba3 occurrence will close by merge-forward, not a separate fix." ;
  triage:deferredNote "fenix's disposition settled (ATM 2026-09-12T05:10:27Z): correction to the above -- BA.3 has carried the no-delivery-channel warn since 67ff0420f (herdr_queue_wake_reminders.rs:247, one warn per candidate per tick, bare return), so the production half was already present and is on BA.3 at c462c6977 (BA3-QA2 verifies it, tracked like BA3-QA1-001/002/003). Only the missing test still lands on fix/phase-ba-cleanup (cipher, BA-CLEANUP-FIXUP)." ;
  triage:promoteTo "fix/phase-ba-cleanup" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T03:23:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
